  },
  "note": "Election of the Donaghadee Urban Council, May 1955. Only seven candidates were nominated for nine seats, so all were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1955, p. 6). The seven were: South Ward - Mrs. E. J. Boyd, Mrs. A. M. Webb, Mr. Joseph Wilson Shannon, Mr. Alex. Girvan; North Ward - Mr. Gordon Arthur Phillips, Capt. W. Joseph Long, Mr. Charles C. Stewart. Messrs. J. J. M'Conkey and J. A. M'Cullough, retiring members, were to be invited to fill the two vacancies. Returned unopposed."
